WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.420
Dear brothers, sisters, and friends, hello. I’m Wang Jialing.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:12.860
I was deeply moved by the two sisters who shared. I believe they have found the meaning of life.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:23.570
Today’s good news is that God can be known. When we find God, we find the meaning of our existence.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:29.940
The God we know is not a god we made, but the God who made us.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:37.520
The universe does not begin with you or me, or with our needs. It begins with God.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:45.100
Without meeting God, our lives drift without a fixed direction.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.100
We are like a boat, not knowing where to drift or where to anchor.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:01:01.420
But the two sisters and I can testify: we have found where we belong.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:12.680
At university, I teach graduate students decision-making—how to make decisions.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:20.040
More than forty years ago, after university, I decided to seek my Creator.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:35.760
At the time, I asked myself a question that I felt no one could properly answer.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.080
Why do I exist?

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:50.480
In the first sister’s testimony, that same question led her to explore and seek an answer.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:59.820
I believe many friends, brothers, and sisters here have asked: Why do I exist?

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:04.480
Philosophers say we came into existence without a choice.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:13.160
Our parents did not ask whether we wanted to come into this world. We simply arrived.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.860
We did not choose to come into existence.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:22.160
One day, we will also have to leave this world.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:32.620
When death comes, no one can overcome it or choose its time and manner.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:41.260
Leaving aside suicide—life is too precious; as Christians, we would not choose that path.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.420
We will all have to leave this world.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:52.530
If we cannot choose our birth or death, must we simply drift helplessly through the time between?

00:02:52.530 --> 00:03:01.410
But is that all life is? Must we live it helplessly?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:08.550
That was the question I asked at twenty-two, graduating from university with everything going well.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:14.940
I graduated from National Taiwan University and was chosen to speak on behalf of the graduates.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.900
My grades were very good, and I received a full scholarship to study in the United States.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.120
For a sociology student, this was a rare opportunity.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:31.830
My family was loving. Our parents loved us, the four siblings were close, and we were financially comfortable.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.890
I had many classmates, both men and women, and we got along very well.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:43.290
I felt like a passenger in the first-class cabin of a plane.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:52.250
But I asked: Where is this plane going? Is it really flying where I want to go?

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:58.370
Everyone seemed to envy the wonderful seat I had up in the sky.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:05.090
Yet I wondered: Will this plane really land where I want to be?

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:09.740
What, then, should I pursue in life?

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:20.220
The best decision of my life was to actively seek my Creator while life was going well.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:26.800
Life still brings challenges, but I no longer see them as bad luck.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.780
Every experience can help me know Christ and experience Him.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:38.180
To me, all of this has enriched my life. I truly thank the Lord.
